[ext_resource type="Script" uid="uid://dd85gxidfhqxl" path="res://systems/dialogue/dialogue_data.gd" id="1_dlg"]

[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_dlg")
source = "# Tinker Hex: trader. Sarcastic, fair. Gives Salvage Rights (Act I) and The Overflow (Act II).
# Use on a ShopNPC so 'open_shop' works. Reminders and declines fall through to the shop.
~ start
# A Yard Sweep deleted Hex's spare cells (YardCrates CargoA): said once; the shop sells two less
@ crate_news:CargoA -> loss_cells
@ quest_ready:clear_hub -> ready_clear_hub
@ quest_active:clear_hub -> remind_clear_hub
@ can_start:clear_hub -> offer_clear_hub
@ quest_ready:q04_the_overflow -> ready_q04_the_overflow
@ quest_active:q04_the_overflow -> remind_q04_the_overflow
@ can_start:q04_the_overflow -> offer_q04_the_overflow
@ quest_ready:copied_stock -> ready_copied_stock
@ quest_active:copied_stock -> remind_copied_stock
@ can_start:copied_stock -> offer_copied_stock
@ quest_ready:static_from_home -> ready_static
@ quest_active:static_from_home -> remind_static
@ can_start:static_from_home -> offer_static
# Act V: Hex came along (Root Access). One-time lines in the Core ('said' deeds)
@ quest_done:q08_null_gatekeeper -> core
-> idle

~ core
@ !deed:said:hex_core -> core_first
@ quest_done:q10_root_process -> core_end
@ deed:said:vesper_packet -> core_packet_check
@ quest_done:paged_out -> core_paged_check
-> idle

~ core_first
> report said hex_core
Hex: Shop's open. Don't ask what currency they use down here. I'm still charging in ours.
Hex: Credits are worth exactly what someone will sell you for them. Down here, that's me. So they're worth a lot.
Hex: I said nobody sells anything past the gate, and that's why I came. I didn't say I'd like it.
-> idle

~ core_packet_check
@ !deed:said:hex_packet -> core_packet
@ quest_done:paged_out -> core_paged_check
-> idle

~ core_packet
> report said hex_packet
Hex: Vesper's been looking at me funny. Like she read something she shouldn't have.
Hex: If it's about the packet, I don't want to know. Brack's voice is Brack's voice. That's all I'm keeping.
-> idle

~ core_paged_check
@ !deed:said:hex_paged -> core_paged
-> idle

~ core_paged
> report said hex_paged
Hex: Paged out. So that's where things go when nobody's holding on to them. Explains my inventory.
-> idle

~ core_end
@ deed:ending:any -> core_after
Hex: Whatever you pick down there, I want it in writing. A receipt. Something.
-> idle

~ core_after
Hex: You picked. I'm still here, so I'm calling it a good sale.
-> idle

~ offer_static
Hex: Hardfault's been pinging the relay for days. Brack, mostly. None of it gets here.
Hex: I traced it. The calls fall into those wells south-east of here and bounce round forever. Wisps carry them.
Hex: Bring them back. Not because I miss anyone. Because they owe me money.
* ACCEPT -> accept_static
* DECLINE -> idle

~ accept_static
> start_quest static_from_home
Hex: Three packets. The wisps learn whatever hits them, so don't hit them the same way twice.
-> end

~ remind_static
Hex: Still static. Three packets, Echo Wells.
-> idle

~ ready_static
> turn_in static_from_home
Hex: That's Brack. That's me. That's... that's Brack's voice, and I don't know what he's saying.
Hex: Don't tell him. Next time he calls, I'll pretend it came through clean.
-> end

~ offer_copied_stock
Hex: Somebody copied my inventory. I want royalties.
Hex: Four crates at Mirror Dock, carried round by those husks. Same scratches, same price tags. Mine, exactly.
* ACCEPT -> accept_copied_stock
* DECLINE -> idle

~ accept_copied_stock
> start_quest copied_stock
Hex: They shrug off the same trick twice. Bring a script that can change its mind.
-> end

~ remind_copied_stock
Hex: Four crates. I counted them before they existed.
-> idle

~ ready_copied_stock
Hex: That's them. Don't tell me how they smell the same.
* TURN IN -> turnin_copied_stock
* NOT YET -> idle

~ turnin_copied_stock
> turn_in copied_stock
Hex: Paid in full. The originals go on my shelf, and the copies go on sale. Half price. Same scratches.
Hex: Nobody sells anything past that gate, which is why I'm going.
-> idle

~ offer_clear_hub
# NEW: Act I quest, not in the campaign doc
Hex: So you're what crawled out of the outer ward. Good. I need someone expendable.
Hex: Two Corrupted are squatting on my supply caches. One in the Spillway, one in the Cache Warrens.
* ACCEPT -> accept_clear_hub
* DECLINE -> idle

~ accept_clear_hub
> start_quest clear_hub
Hex: Clear them out. I get my caches back, you get paid, and we both complain less.
-> end

~ remind_clear_hub
Hex: My caches are still occupied. Raider in the Spillway, Enchanter in the Warrens.
-> idle

~ ready_clear_hub
Hex: Caches clear?
* TURN IN -> turnin_clear_hub
* NOT YET -> idle

~ turnin_clear_hub
> turn_in clear_hub
Hex: Sixty credits. Don't spend it all in one place. Unless the place is my shop.
-> start

~ offer_q04_the_overflow
Hex: A big crawler is sitting on all my power cells. Kill it and I’ll pay well.
* ACCEPT -> accept_q04_the_overflow
* DECLINE -> end

~ accept_q04_the_overflow
> start_quest q04_the_overflow
Hex: It's out in the Signal Wastes. And it's a buffer, not a bug: five slots, and nobody ever checked the bounds.
# The Overflow's lock (OverflowLock): one cast that lands more hits than the buffer holds
Hex: Hit it once, it files it away. Hit it five times in one go, it files that too. Six in one cast and it runs off the end.
Hex: Loop something all the way to the cap. When it overflows it spills, so either step back or have a shield scripted.
-> end

~ remind_q04_the_overflow
# NEW line below
Hex: My cells are still under that thing.
# NEW line below
Hex: Six hits, one cast. Five it can hold.

~ ready_q04_the_overflow
Hex: Done?
* TURN IN -> turnin_q04_the_overflow
* NOT YET -> end

~ turnin_q04_the_overflow
> turn_in q04_the_overflow
Hex: My cells! Here’s your reward. A better weapon, as promised.
-> start

~ loss_cells
> report crate_mourned CargoA
Hex: My spare cells. Tagged, swept, gone. Half my stock ran off those.
Hex: Shelf's thinner till I get them back. Word is C-0 keeps what it deletes in a queue, in the Sweep, till it gets round to burning it.
Hex: If you're passing a cage with my scratches on it, I'm not asking. I'm hinting very loudly.
-> start

~ idle
Hex: Buying, selling, complaining. Pick two.
* TRADE -> shop
* GOODBYE -> end

~ shop
Hex: Trading is simple. You offer, I offer, we both complain.
> open_shop"
